The dev database is at the release being worked on: it opened with
`@release 4` before the drop was written. A line of release 4 applies to a
database at 4, so adding one mid-release needs no bump.

== before
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL, note TEXT) STRICT;
INSERT INTO dish VALUES (1, 'soup', 'hot');
PRAGMA user_version = 4;

== after
-- @release 4
-- @drop 4 column dish note
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT;

== plan
roux: migrating test.db, 4 steps
  table `dish`: aside, to make it anew
    ALTER TABLE "dish" RENAME TO "roux_old_dish"
  table `dish`: as schema.sql makes it
    CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT
  table `dish`: its rows, by id, name
    INSERT INTO "dish" ("id", "name") SELECT "id", "name" FROM "roux_old_dish"
  table `dish`: the old one
    DROP TABLE "roux_old_dish"
migrated from release 4
